// A LIVE rig: something plugged in, heard through this machine.
//
// It declares no `surfaces/` — no timeline, no viewport, no desk — and that is the whole
// of what makes it this shape rather than another. A project draws what it DECLARES, so
// this one opens on its graph and nothing else. See packages/song/docs/liveProject.md.
//
// It holds no material either: no `clips/`, no `sequences/`. Nothing is arranged, so
// nothing warns about an arrangement that is not drawn.
project({
  name: "live",
  // Kept although nothing is arranged: the metronome counts in it, and so does a
  // delay whose time is written in beats.
  tempo: 120,
  sampleRate: 48000,
})
